WEBVTT

NOTE calculation-settings: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.461
Three numbers decide every suggestion
on the course: the daily maximum,

V0-2
00:00:06.561 --> 00:00:09.280
the Lynx reference amount,
and the crop coefficient.

V1a-1
00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:17.554
The gear button opens the dialog
on Calculation by default.

V1a-2
00:00:17.654 --> 00:00:21.368
If you last arrived through Review
Threshold, it opens on Minimum

V1a-3
00:00:21.468 --> 00:00:25.413
Threshold instead, and the tab is
sticky for the rest of the session.

V1b-1
00:00:25.933 --> 00:00:29.407
This is the Calculation tab.
These are site-level settings,

V1b-2
00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:31.863
so they apply to every user on the site.

V2a-1
00:00:39.176 --> 00:00:43.659
Daily Max Amount is the most water
Spatial Adjust will ask for in one day,

V2a-2
00:00:43.759 --> 00:00:46.546
in your own units,
up to a hard ceiling of 15.

V2b-1
00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:52.322
Every station whose deficit exceeds this
lands on the same suggested percentage,

V2b-2
00:00:52.422 --> 00:00:55.420
which is why identical
numbers appear in runs.

V3a-1
00:01:03.286 --> 00:01:08.013
Lynx Reference Amount is the amount of
water a station applies at 100 percent

V3a-2
00:01:08.113 --> 00:01:13.086
adjust. The suggested percentage is the
applied amount divided by this reference.

V3b-1
00:01:13.603 --> 00:01:17.490
Set it too low and every
suggestion looks enormous:

V3b-2
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:23.611
a 10 mm cap against a 3 mm reference
gives a maximum suggestion of 333 percent.

V3b-3
00:01:23.711 --> 00:01:28.743
In Lynx, Next Amount must equal
this reference, in the same units.

V4a-1
00:01:36.143 --> 00:01:40.091
Crop Coefficient is a whole-number
percentage from 0 to 200,

V4a-2
00:01:40.191 --> 00:01:43.943
applied to the day's ET before
it enters the calculation.

V4b-1
00:01:44.493 --> 00:01:50.484
Below 100, the course is treated as using
less water than reference ET suggests;

V4b-2
00:01:50.584 --> 00:01:54.778
above 100, more. Under Option
1 the dialog greys it out,

V4b-3
00:01:54.878 --> 00:01:58.923
along with Daily Max Amount
and Lynx Reference Amount.

V5a-1
00:02:05.346 --> 00:02:09.680
Save Changes sends the settings, asks
the server to recalculate adjustments,

V5a-2
00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.716
and reloads the dashboard so that
area and hole averages are rebuilt.

V5b-1
00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:19.174
A new Lynx Reference Amount rescales
every suggestion above zero.

V5b-2
00:02:19.274 --> 00:02:23.673
A new Daily Max Amount moves only
the stations at the old or new cap,

V5b-3
00:02:23.773 --> 00:02:29.130
and stations at zero usually stay there. A
% Adj. you typed earlier keeps its value.
